{{feat
|type=special
|prereq=[[fighter]], [[base attack bonus]] +4, [[weapon focus]] (chosen weapon)
|reqfor=[[epic weapon specialization]]
|desc=A [[character]] with this [[feat]] has trained especially hard with a specific [[weapon]] type, and gains a +2 damage bonus when using these weapons in combat.
|use=This feat may be selected multiple times, but the effects do not [[stack]]. It applies to a new weapon in each case.
|special=[[Halfling]]s and [[gnome]]s are small creatures and as such they can never use the following large weapons: [[dire mace]], [[two-bladed sword]], [[double axe]], [[greataxe]], [[greatsword]], [[halberd]], [[heavy flail]], and [[scythe]].
|bonus1=fighter
}}__NOTOC__

==Notes==
*This feat can only be chosen when gaining a fighter level.
*Four fighter levels are required to take this feat, not merely being a (multiclassed) fighter with a base attack of 4.

===Previous versions===
*Prior to version 1.69, only a single fighter level was required to take ''weapon specialization'' in the [[club]].

==Builder notes==
'''Item feat:''' Only for unarmed, but the others can be added with custom content.

==Custom content notes==
'''Removable:''' yes

'''Reusable:''' yes

'''Script:''' hardcoded

*These feats can be added to [[iprp_feats.2da]] to make them available as item feats.
*A custom class must have this feat in their feat list, or that class will not be able to select it as a general feat.

